{
  "esm": "1.3.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "mom6_cgrid_bound_coriolis_u",
    "description": "The bound_coriolis east-face Coriolis + momentum-advection acceleration of the mom6_cgrid: CAu(i,j,k) = clamp(pvf_u(i,j,k), min(fv1..fv4), max(fv1..fv4)) - KEx(i,j,k), the MOM_CoriolisAdv.F90 CorAdCalc bound_Coriolis law (the fv1..fv4 bounds and the min/max clamp at :897-925, then the -d(KE)/dx term of the KEx loop at :930-940): fv1 = av(i,j,k)*v(i+1,j,k), fv2 = av(i,j,k)*v(i,j,k), fv3 = av(i,j-1,k)*v(i+1,j-1,k), fv4 = av(i,j-1,k)*v(i,j-1,k), the av*v products at the four q-points around the east face (av the absolute vorticity at the q-points, v the north-face velocities of the two cells on each side of the face), with the raw potential-vorticity flux pvf_u (the sibling mom6_cgrid_pvf_u rule) clamped to the local bound and the zonal KE gradient KEx subtracted (clamp(x, lo, hi) = min(max(x, lo), hi) is exact — max/min select without rounding, so the Fortran's min-then-max sequence produces identical bits). SOLID-WALL BOUNDARIES: the east domain edge (i = N_I) and the south domain edge (j = 1) carry a zero-gradient halo, so the wall regions MIRROR the out-of-bounds neighbor onto the edge cell itself: the i = N_I region reads v(N_I,j,k) in place of v(N_I+1,j,k) and the j = 1 region reads av(i,1,k) in place of av(i,0,k) (the SE corner mirrors both) — NOT clamped reads of nonexistent cells. The rule is a named-op rule (esm-spec 9.6.8), applied once per consumer equation as mom6_cgrid_bound_coriolis_u(pvf_u, av, v, KEx); all four params must be declared [i,j,k] fields (esm-spec 9.6.1 where clause).",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:rule",
      "family:mom6_cgrid",
      "grid:mom6_cgrid",
      "op:clamp",
      "order:0",
      "bc:wall",
      "axes:i,j,k"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Adcroft, A., et al. (2019). The GFDL global ocean and sea ice model OM4.0. Journal of Advances in Modeling Earth Systems, 11(10), 3167-3211.",
        "doi": "10.1029/2019MS001726"
      },
      {
        "citation": "MOM6 source: MOM_CoriolisAdv.F90 CorAdCalc bound_Coriolis fv1..fv4 :897-925 and the -d(KE)/dx term :930-940; the face conventions of the mom6_cgrid grid.esm."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "../grid.esm"
    }
  ],
